r/14063974/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-102705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2x+2y=1 \\\\ 2x-3y=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063974/state.json" "file_sha256" "61a1f2a40c8bf0b5c68fa4fd80cae8b8fa5c849c473d44adf44ddf74746e6793" "basis" 2086 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063974/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-102705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(-2)\\cdot (-3)-2\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063974/state.json" "file_sha256" "61a1f2a40c8bf0b5c68fa4fd80cae8b8fa5c849c473d44adf44ddf74746e6793" "basis" 2086 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063974/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-102705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.diff